Dagster OSS on EKS — Multi-Project Platform Runbook

Scope: Production-ready reference for running Dagster OSS on EKS with multiple data science / ingestion projects, two Helm charts (platform + code-location), two ArgoCD ApplicationSets with git-file-generator seeding, Kargo image promotion, and dg workspace local dev.

Version discipline: Dagster core 1.13.x, integration libs 0.29.x, pinned in one place (platform_common). Webserver/daemon and every code-location image MUST run the same core minor version.

Design principles:
1. One image per project = dependency isolation (torch vs. legacy sklearn never conflict).
2. One generic code-location chart, instantiated N times by a values file per project per env. The values file is the onboarding seed.
3. All env/project differences are injected env vars (EnvVar() in code, ConfigMap/ExternalSecret in K8s, .env locally). Zero if env  "prod" in Python.
4. Platform and code locations are decoupled through one contract: the dagster-workspace ConfigMap.
⸻
1. Architecture

                        ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                        │  ArgoCD                                      │
                        │  AppSet #1: platform  (generator: envs)      │
                        │  AppSet #2: locations (generator: git files  │
                        │             projects/*/deploy/values-*.yaml) │
                        └───────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘
                                        │ sync
        namespace: dagster-<env>        ▼
 ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  PLATFORM (chart: platform, wraps official dagster chart)           │
 │   ├── dagster-webserver ──reads── ConfigMap: dagster-workspace      │
 │   ├── dagster-daemon    (QueuedRunCoordinator, K8sRunLauncher)      │
 │   └── instance: RDS Postgres + S3 compute logs (dagster.yaml        │
 │       fully generated from Helm values — never hand-edited)         │
 │                                                                     │
 │  CODE LOCATIONS (chart: code-location, one release per project)     │
 │   ├── ds-churn        gRPC :4000  (image: ecr/ds-churn:<sha>)       │
 │   ├── ds-forecasting  gRPC :4000  (image: ecr/ds-forecasting:<sha>) │
 │   └── ingestion       gRPC :4000  (image: ecr/ingestion:<sha>)      │
 │        │                                                            │
 │        └── K8sRunLauncher spawns run pods FROM THE SAME IMAGE,      │
 │            with env/secrets/resources propagated via                │
 │            DAGSTER_CLI_API_GRPC_CONTAINER_CONTEXT                   │
 └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

 Image flow:  git push → CI (path-filtered matrix) → ECR
              → Kargo Warehouse detects tag → Stage dev (auto) writes
                tag into values-dev.yaml → Stage prod (gated) writes
                tag into values-prod.yaml → ArgoCD syncs


Namespace rule: platform + all code locations of one environment live in the same namespace (dagster-dev, dagster-prod). The run launcher, instance ConfigMap, and Postgres secret references assume this. Do not split.
