3. Shared library: platform_common

This package is the compatibility layer. It pins dagster core so projects cannot drift, and it must include the instance/storage deps that both the gRPC server process and the launched run pods need at runtime.

libs/platform_common/pyproject.toml:

[project]
name = "platform-common"
version = "0.4.0"
requires-python = ">=3.12"
dependencies = [
    "dagster1.13.*",          # THE core pin — projects inherit this
    "dagster-postgres0.29.*", # REQUIRED in every image: code servers and
    "dagster-aws0.29.*",      # run pods talk to the instance (RDS + S3)
    "dagster-k8s0.29.*",
    "pydantic>=2",
]

[build-system]
requires = ["hatchling"]
build-backend = "hatchling.build"


Why dagster-postgres/aws in every image: sensor and schedule evaluation executes inside the code-location gRPC process using an instance ref passed by the daemon; run pods write events straight to Postgres and logs to S3. If a project image lacks these libs, sensors and runs fail with import errors that look like platform problems. Bake them into the shared pin and forget about it.

libs/platform_common/src/platform_common/resources.py (pattern excerpt):

from dagster import ConfigurableResource, EnvVar
from dagster_aws.s3 import S3PickleIOManager, S3Resource


class HttpSourceConfig(ConfigurableResource):
    """Generic ingestion source. Per-project values come from env."""
    endpoint: str
    bucket: str
    api_key: str


def make_s3_io_manager(prefix_env: str = "S3_IO_PREFIX"):
    return S3PickleIOManager(
        s3_resource=S3Resource(region_name=EnvVar("AWS_REGION")),
        s3_bucket=EnvVar("DAGSTER_IO_BUCKET"),
        s3_prefix=EnvVar(prefix_env),
    )

