4.2 projects/ds-churn/src/ds_churn/definitions.py

from dagster import Definitions, EnvVar
from platform_common.resources import HttpSourceConfig, make_s3_io_manager

from ds_churn.assets import all_assets

defs = Definitions(
    assets=all_assets,
    resources={
        "io_manager": make_s3_io_manager(),
        "source": HttpSourceConfig(
            endpoint=EnvVar("CHURN_SRC_ENDPOINT"),
            bucket=EnvVar("CHURN_RAW_BUCKET"),
            api_key=EnvVar("CHURN_API_KEY"),
        ),
    },
)


EnvVar resolves at run-launch time, not import time — same code works with .env locally and ConfigMap/Secret on EKS, and secrets never bake into snapshots.

4.3 projects/ds-churn/Dockerfile

FROM python:3.12-slim AS base
ENV UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE=1 UV_LINK_MODE=copy
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir uv

WORKDIR /app
# Shared lib first (better layer caching when only project code changes)
COPY libs/platform_common /libs/platform_common
COPY projects/ds-churn/pyproject.toml projects/ds-churn/uv.lock ./
RUN uv sync --frozen --no-install-project

COPY projects/ds-churn/src ./src
RUN uv sync --frozen

ENV PATH="/app/.venv/bin:$PATH"
EXPOSE 4000
# NOTE: no CMD args for host/port here that differ per env — keep it static
CMD ["dagster", "api", "grpc", "-h", "0.0.0.0", "-p", "4000", \
     "-m", "ds_churn.definitions"]


Build context is the repo root (so libs/ is copyable): docker build -f projects/ds-churn/Dockerfile .

4.4 The seed: projects/ds-churn/deploy/values-prod.yaml

This single file is everything ArgoCD needs to deploy the location. Committing it is the deployment action.

locationName: ds-churn
moduleName: ds_churn.definitions

image:
  repository: 123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/dagster/ds-churn
  tag: "git-0000000"            # managed by Kargo — do not hand-edit in prod

codeServer:
  replicas: 1
  resources:
    requests: { cpu: 250m, memory: 512Mi }
    limits:   { memory: 1Gi }

# Non-secret, per-project, per-env config → ConfigMap → pod env
env:
  AWS_REGION: us-west-2
  DAGSTER_IO_BUCKET: srca-aiops-dagster-prod
  S3_IO_PREFIX: ds-churn
  CHURN_SRC_ENDPOINT: https://api.vendor.com/v2
  CHURN_RAW_BUCKET: srca-aiops-raw-prod

# Secrets via External Secrets Operator → K8s Secret → pod env
secrets:
  enabled: true
  storeRef: aws-parameter-store        # ClusterSecretStore name
  items:
    - envName: CHURN_API_KEY
      remoteKey: /dagster/prod/ds-churn/api-key

# Propagated to RUN PODS (not the gRPC server) via container context
runK8sConfig:
  container_config:
    resources:
      requests: { cpu: "1", memory: 4Gi }
      limits:   { memory: 8Gi }
  pod_spec_config:
    node_selector: { workload: batch }

serviceAccount: dagster-code-location   # IRSA role with S3 + source access


Name mapping to your actual repo (aiops-dagster): in this document platform_common = your shared package, ds-churn = your data_science project, and 1.13.* should be your exact 1.13.5 pin (exact pins + full uv.lock resolution is strictly better — keep it). One adjustment worth making: your data-science package currently depends on dagster-webserver and dagster-dg-cli. Those are needed for local dg dev only, not for the gRPC image. Move them to a dev group so the production image stays lean:

[dependency-groups]
dev = ["dagster-webserver1.13.5", "dagster-dg-cli1.13.5"]


Then in the Dockerfile use uv sync --frozen --no-dev. Locally, uv sync installs everything.
