10. Kargo — image promotion (dev auto, prod gated)

One Warehouse + two Stages per project. Kargo watches ECR, writes the tag into the seed values file, and Argo does the rest.

deploy/kargo/project.yaml:

apiVersion: kargo.akuity.io/v1alpha1
kind: Project
metadata:
  name: aiops-dagster


deploy/kargo/data-science/warehouse.yaml:

apiVersion: kargo.akuity.io/v1alpha1
kind: Warehouse
metadata:
  name: data-science
  namespace: aiops-dagster
spec:
  subscriptions:
    - image:
        repoURL: 123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/dagster/data-science
        imageSelectionStrategy: NewestBuild
        allowTags: ^git-


deploy/kargo/data-science/stage-dev.yaml:

apiVersion: kargo.akuity.io/v1alpha1
kind: Stage
metadata:
  name: data-science-dev
  namespace: aiops-dagster
spec:
  requestedFreight:
    - origin: { kind: Warehouse, name: data-science }
      sources: { direct: true }
  promotionTemplate:
    spec:
      steps:
        - uses: git-clone
          config:
            repoURL: https://github.com/srca/aiops-dagster
            checkout: [{ branch: main, path: ./repo }]
        - uses: yaml-update
          config:
            path: ./repo/projects/data-science/deploy/values-dev.yaml
            updates:
              - key: image.tag
                value: ${{ imageFrom("123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/dagster/data-science").Tag }}
        - uses: git-commit
          config:
            path: ./repo
            message: "kargo: data-science dev → ${{ imageFrom(\"123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/dagster/data-science\").Tag }}"
        - uses: git-push
          config: { path: ./repo }
        - uses: argocd-update
          config:
            apps: [{ name: dg-loc-data-science-dev }]


stage-prod.yaml is identical except: requestedFreight[0].sources: { stages: [data-science-dev] } (freight must pass through dev first), the yaml-update path targets values-prod.yaml, and no auto-promotion policy — promotion is a manual click/kargo promote, which is your prod gate. Optionally attach an AnalysisTemplate verification on the dev stage (e.g., a smoke job that materializes one canary asset) so freight is only prod-eligible after a green check.

Kargo has no ApplicationSet-style generator yet, so the per-project manifests are stamped from a template — add a make kargo-scaffold PROJECT=x target that renders warehouse + two stages with envsubst. Verify step syntax against your installed Kargo minor version; the steps API stabilized in v1 but field names have shifted between minors.
⸻
11. Local development (dg workspace)

Root dg.toml:

directory_type = "workspace"

[workspace]
[[workspace.projects]]
path = "projects/data-science"
[[workspace.projects]]
path = "projects/ingestion"


Daily loop for a DS engineer:

cd projects/data-science
cp .env.example .env        # fill in local values, same keys as the ConfigMap
uv sync                     # installs dev group incl. dagster-webserver
cd ../.. && dg dev          # all locations, one UI, per-project venvs


Rules that keep local↔EKS parity exact:

- .env.example in every project is the authoritative list of required env vars. The seed values file (env: + secrets.items[].envName) must cover the same keys. A 10-line CI script can diff the two and fail the PR on drift — cheap insurance against "works locally, crashes on EKS."
- Local uses SQLite instance + filesystem IO by default under dg dev; if an asset needs S3 locally, point DAGSTER_IO_BUCKET at a dev bucket in .env. No code changes either way.
- Never run the webserver from a project venv against prod Postgres. Local is local.
⸻
12. Onboarding checklist — new project (~15 min, one PR)

1. uvx create-dagster@latest project projects/<name> (adds itself to dg.toml).
2. Add platform-common/shared path dep + your project deps → uv lock.
3. Copy a neighbor's Dockerfile, change the module name.
4. Write deploy/values-dev.yaml + deploy/values-prod.yaml (the seeds). Tag can start at any pushed image.
5. Add one line to charts/workspace-configmap/values-{dev,prod}.yaml.
6. Create the SSM/Parameter Store entries referenced in secrets.items.
7. make kargo-scaffold PROJECT=<name>.
8. Merge. CI builds the image, AppSet #2 creates the Application, reloader restarts the webserver, location appears.

Nothing in the platform chart, ArgoCD config, or CI pipeline is touched. That's the low-toil payoff.
⸻
13. Day-2 operations

Dagster upgrade (e.g. 1.13.5 → 1.14.x) — the only genuinely careful procedure:

1. One PR: bump dagster== pin in shared, run make lock-all (re-locks every project), bump charts/platform/Chart.yaml dependency version to match.
2. Merge → CI rebuilds all images (libs/ change triggers full matrix).
3. Promote all locations through dev via Kargo; verify.
4. Prod order: set migrate.enabled: true on platform → sync platform (runs dagster instance migrate job) → promote all locations → set migrate.enabled: false.
5. Never leave webserver and code servers skewed across a minor version overnight.

Rollback one project: git revert the Kargo tag-bump commit for that seed file (or promote older freight). Argo self-heals. Platform and other projects untouched.

Rollback platform: revert the platform values/chart PR. Note: instance schema migrations are forward-only — snapshot RDS before step 4 above.

Lockfile hygiene (your 2500-line locks): the lock is the contract; treat it as code. uv lock --check in CI (already in §9) blocks drift. Use Renovate/Dependabot grouped monthly PRs for non-dagster deps per project; dagster-family bumps only ever happen via the shared pin + lock-all so versions can never fork between projects. Makefile:

lock-all:
	for p in projects/*/; do (cd $$p && uv lock); done


Observability minimums: alert on daemon heartbeat (webserver /server_info + daemon liveness), code-location readiness (a location down = its sensors/schedules silently stopped), QueuedRunCoordinator queue depth, and RDS connections (each code server + run pod holds connections — set max_connections headroom and consider RDS Proxy past ~10 locations).
⸻
14. Troubleshooting
Symptom	Cause	Fix
New location not in UI	Webserver hasn't re-read workspace CM	Reloader annotation missing (§7.2), or restart deploy/dagster-webserver
Location shows "loading error" after deploy	Rollout race: webserver hit gRPC before ready	Readiness probe (§5.4) prevents; click "Reload" in UI
Sensors fail with ModuleNotFoundError: dagster_postgres	Instance libs missing from project image	They belong in shared deps (§3) — never per-project
Run pods start but have no project env/secrets	Container context env missing on code server	DAGSTER_CLI_API_GRPC_CONTAINER_CONTEXT (§5.3/5.4)
Run pod uses wrong/latest image	DAGSTER_CURRENT_IMAGE not set	§5.4
gRPC errors on large asset graphs	Default 50MB message cap	Set DAGSTER_GRPC_MAX_RX_BYTES (e.g. 104857600) on webserver, daemon, and code servers
Deserialization error / snapshot mismatch	Version skew webserver vs code server	Re-align to the single pin; check image.tag vs platform chart version
Everything vanished from UI at once	Workspace CM renamed/deleted	CM name dagster-workspace is load-bearing (§6.2) — keep stable across refactors
Runs stuck QUEUED	Concurrency limits or daemon down	Check daemon logs + coordinator config (§7.2)
Run pods Pending forever	runK8sConfig nodeSelector matches no nodes / no Karpenter provisioner	Fix selector or provisioner requirements
Secret env empty in pod	ExternalSecret not synced	kubectl describe externalsecret <loc>-secrets; check ClusterSecretStore IRSA
CI green, EKS crashloop on import	.env.example ↔ values drift	Run the parity check (§11); missing key in env: map
uv sync --frozen fails in Docker	pyproject changed without re-lock	uv lock --check gate (§9) should have caught it pre-merge
